RD BLUR-TARGET SIZES (SSAO/SSIL; GDScript cannot query RD textures, so derived per engine behavior from the measured live sizes above)
  SSAO: NO targets anywhere on this route. Zero `ssao_enabled = true` sites exist under game/src (grep).
  SSIL (allocated at half the viewport's 3D render size = size * scaling_3d_scale / 2):
    main_menu: render 1280x720*0.75 = 960x540 -> SSIL targets 480x270. HEALTHY.
    mission_prep: render 2x2*1.0 = 2x2 -> SSIL targets 1x1. DEGENERATE (below mip minimum; see cascade below).
    guildhall mission main view: render 1280x720 (window scaling 1.0; SSIL on via weather_profile.gd:420 desktop path) -> SSIL targets 640x360. HEALTHY.
    wardrobe x2: SSIL off -> no targets.
  SSR trace buffers (render size): main_menu 960x540; mission_prep 2x2; mission 1280x720 (weather_profile.gd:453).
  Glow mip chain: main_menu from 960x540, 5 levels (main_menu.gd glow_level loop); mission_prep from 2x2 (feeds the mipmap errors); mission den/guildhall per mission_controller.gd:291-302 caps; mobile caps per mobile_profile.gd apply_environment (checked, no viewport sizing there); weather_visuals.gd builds sky/rain only (checked, no env toggles, no viewports).
  Godot issue context: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/86631 -- "SubViewport with BOTH x and y < 32px + SSIL enabled => render_scene_buffers_rd null-texture error spam". The (2,2)+SSIL prep viewport is exactly that trigger.

