NOT-A-PROBE-ARTIFACT PROOF (parentage micro-run, same temp file, NVIDIA GPU)
  Stage A (prep parented to root Window, as in the first probe): prep.size=(0,0), container=(0,0), viewport=(2,2).
  Stage B (prep parented to a CanvasLayer): prep.size=(0,0), container=(0,0), viewport=(2,2).
  Real game parentage == Stage B: ContractTableUI extends CanvasLayer (contract_table_ui.gd:1) and does add_child(prep) (contract_table_ui.gd:518). So the shipped prep screen crushes its 3D rooftop backdrop to the (2,2) engine-minimum clamp the same way.

VERDICT: container-crush CONFIRMED, tiny-blur-target REJECTED.
  The (2,2) is not an authored small size and no RD target is authored small: the authored prep size is (1280,720) (mission_prep_ui.gd:163) but its zero-size container (0,0) crushes the child to the (2,2) floor at runtime, and that crushed SSIL viewport emits the 86631 cascade. All healthy viewports derive healthy half-res targets (480x270, 640x360). No game/src content was modified by this probe.
  GPU-required claim: CLOSED. The route ran under live Vulkan Forward+ on a real NVIDIA GPU (see adapter line); Xvfb supplied only the X display. Nothing is left open for lack of GPU.
